{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB14568 - MONDO_18433",
  "verbalization": "Ivosidenib is being considered for repurposing in the treatment of Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) with the translocation T(6;9)(p23;q34), a genetic abnormality associated with AML. The evidence suggests that Ivosidenib may have a role in this disease, as it is indicated for Inherited AML, which is linked to AML with the T(6;9) translocation. This relationship is supported by the indirect pathways through which Ivosidenib may exert its effects, such as through the inhibition of certain enzymes or pathways that are dysregulated in AML. The presence of multiple indirect pathways involving different drugs and indications further supports the potential for Ivosidenib to influence the disease process in this context. However, the exact mechanism by which Ivosidenib affects AML with the T(6;9) translocation remains to be fully elucidated, and further experimental validation is needed to confirm its therapeutic potential.",
